> 3) The free radical stuff(I am very sceptical of this myself)

I keep fairly up to date on this entire field.  I cannot say first hand about
calorie restriction, as I have no desire to practice it.  I believe that the
studies that have been done on the subject are fairly conclusive that it does
have beneficial effects.  

I think that free radicals (and other chemical/physical effects such as
cross-linking of proteins) doe splay a significant part in the aging process.
 They also pose one the greatest threats to those of us who would like to
become immortal, as the nanotechnology needed to reverse these effects is a
long way down the road.  I must therefore advocate reasonable doses of
antoxidants, as well as certain drugs that prevent the glycolization
(cross-linking) of proteins, such as Aminoguanidine.  Many of the drugs that
are useful in this area must be imported from overseas.  If anyone is
interested I would recommend contacting:  LIfe Extension Services, 558-A
Baltimore Pike, Suite 230, Bel Air, MD 21014.  Here's to immortality :-)

